		<item>
		<title>Big title change takes place at AEW Full Gear</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397586-big-title-change-takes-place-at-aew-full-gear/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397586-big-title-change-takes-place-at-aew-full-gear/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:09:02 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Full Gear]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[IIja Dragonuv]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[National Title]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Tommaso Ciampa]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397586</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>IIja Dragonuv is the new AEW National Champion. Dragonuv ended Tommaso Ciampa&#8217;s seven-day reign as champion, at Saturday&#8217;s&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397586-big-title-change-takes-place-at-aew-full-gear/">Big title change takes place at AEW Full Gear</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">IIja Dragonuv is the new AEW National Champion.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Dragonuv ended Tommaso Ciampa&#8217;s seven-day reign as champion, at Saturday&#8217;s Full Gear in Phoenix, Arizona. Ciampa defeated Andrade El Idolo at last Saturday&#8217;s Collision to win the title. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Below is an excerpt from <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397439-aew-full-gear-results-11-14-26-anarchy-in-the-arena-title-matches-and-more/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Alex Kahrs&#8217; AEW Full Gear recap</a> of how the title change went down.</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Dragunov takes the champ to the top turnbuckle for some headbutts, followed by a superplex sending Ciampa crashing against the canvas. He goes for a D-Bomb, but Ciampa dodges it and connects with a Fujiwara armbar. Ciampa then transitions into a running knee, with Dragunov dodging a second one before taking it the third time around…but it’s only good for two as the challenger kicks out!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Tommaso quickly goes for another armbar, but Dragunov breaks free before connecting with not one but two more D-Bombs to pick up the win! That’s three title changes in a row, folks!</p>
</blockquote>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="zxx" dir="ltr"><a href="https://t.co/sksavCrsee">https://t.co/sksavCrsee</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2121814564660715623?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 15, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em><strong>Jerome&#8217;s thoughts:</strong></em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong><em>Not sure what Tony Khan is thinking with this one. Ciampa&#8217;s reign was essentially a week. In his debut match with AEW on the January 31, 2026 episode of Collision, Ciampa wins the TNT Title from Mark Briscoe, only to turn around and drop the belt 11 days later to Kyle Fletcher.</em></strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong><em>I don&#8217;t understand the very short title reigns Ciampa has had or why even put the title on him, only to turn around and take it off so soon. They could have easily had Dragonuv just beat Andrade instead. </em></strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em><strong>Playing hot potato with titles only hurts the lineage of what they are supposed to represent. </strong></em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397586-big-title-change-takes-place-at-aew-full-gear/">Big title change takes place at AEW Full Gear</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397586-big-title-change-takes-place-at-aew-full-gear/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>New Tag Team Champions Crowned At AEW Full Gear</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397552-new-tag-team-champions-crowned-at-aew-full-gear/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397552-new-tag-team-champions-crowned-at-aew-full-gear/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 03:33:17 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Brawling Birds]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Full Gear]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Women's World Tag Team Champions]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Wrathlander]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397552</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Wrathlander (Harley Cameron and Kris Statlander) are the new AEW Women&#8217;s World Tag Team Champions. Cameron and Statlander&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397552-new-tag-team-champions-crowned-at-aew-full-gear/">New Tag Team Champions Crowned At AEW Full Gear</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Wrathlander (Harley Cameron and Kris Statlander) are the new AEW Women&#8217;s World Tag Team Champions.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cameron and Statlander defeated the Brawling Birds (Jamie Hayter and Alex Windsor) to become the new champions, at Saturday&#8217;s AEW Full Gear, held at the Mortgage Matchup Center in Phoenix, Arizona. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Below is an excerpt from <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397439-aew-full-gear-results-11-14-26-anarchy-in-the-arena-title-matches-and-more/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Alex Kahrs&#8217; AEW Full Gear recap</a> of how the titles changes hands.</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Hayter and Harley go at it off a tag, until Stat gives an assist for a crucifix pin by Harley. Windsor breaks it up just in time and all four women are down. Stat is back up, but gets sent to the outside by the champs as they go after Cameron…but Kris is back in, and gets Windsor on her shoulders. This leads to a chicken fight between Cameron and Windsor until the latter drops Statlander with a reverse rana.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Harley and Jamie are left to trade shots on each other in the ring, with Harley landing a roundhouse kick. Hayter fires back with one of her own, but a Hayterade is blocked with a drop toe hold and a half crab…until Windsor breaks it up! A pair of lariats from Hayter and she goes for the cover…but Kris breaks it up!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Stat with the tag now but she gets set up for Two Birds One Stone…only for Harley to stop Hayter, pulling her out of the ring as Stat drops Windsor to the canvas for the pin and the win!</p>
</blockquote>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="zxx" dir="ltr"><a href="https://t.co/baYusVhpiw">https://t.co/baYusVhpiw</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2121807546583502945?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 15, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397552-new-tag-team-champions-crowned-at-aew-full-gear/">New Tag Team Champions Crowned At AEW Full Gear</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397552-new-tag-team-champions-crowned-at-aew-full-gear/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Titles change hands at AEW Full Gear</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397538-titles-change-hands-at-aew-full-gear/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397538-titles-change-hands-at-aew-full-gear/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 03:12:23 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Full Gear]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[New Level]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Swerve]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Swerve Strickland]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[World Trios Titles]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397538</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Swerve Strickland and New Level (Austin Creed and Kofi) are once again AEW World Trios Champions. Strickland and&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397538-titles-change-hands-at-aew-full-gear/">Titles change hands at AEW Full Gear</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Swerve Strickland and New Level (Austin Creed and Kofi) are once again AEW World Trios Champions.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Strickland and New Level defeated Hangman Page, Brody King and Bandido in a Texas Death Match, at Saturday&#8217;s Full Gear held at the Mortgage Matchup Center in Phoenix, Arizona. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Below is an excerpt from Alex Kahrs&#8217; AEW Full Gear recap of how the title change went down. </p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Bandido follows up with an X-Knee to Swerve’s face before moving the cinder block to the middle of the ring. He looks for a 21 Plex to drive Strickland into it, but New Level stop it before dropping him with what looks like the Big Ending onto the edge of the block instead! Brody King comes running in, bringing New Level to the outside before propping barbed wire table pieces over them for a barricade cross body…only to take a Vertebreaker by Strickland onto the ring steps!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Swerve gets back into the ring, but Page is there as well as he takes out the challenger with a Buckshot Lariat…but a second one is stopped with a chair shot by Strickland! All six men are down as the ref begins the count. It gets to eight as Swerve manages to get to his feet, and right after the count of nine Page is only up enough to take a House Call that knocks him out for the final count! We have new trios champions!</p>
</blockquote>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Hangman, King and Bandido had won the titles from Swerve and New Level at the October 17 WrestleDream PPV. </p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="zxx" dir="ltr"><a href="https://t.co/ivwmuFtK7a">https://t.co/ivwmuFtK7a</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2121801964153610302?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 15, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em><strong>Jerome&#8217;s thoughts</strong>:</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em><strong>Playing hot potato with these titles is making them out to be a joke. It diminishes their value and what they are supposed to represent in tag team wrestling. </strong></em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397538-titles-change-hands-at-aew-full-gear/">Titles change hands at AEW Full Gear</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397538-titles-change-hands-at-aew-full-gear/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Former WWE/NXT tag team debuts at AEW Full Gear</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397497-former-wwe-nxt-tag-team-debuts-at-aew-full-gear/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397497-former-wwe-nxt-tag-team-debuts-at-aew-full-gear/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:23:34 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Creed Brothers]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[debut]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Full Gear]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Kasper Brothers]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[NXT]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397497</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Former WWE tag team and one time NXT tag team champions, the Creed Brothers under their real names&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397497-former-wwe-nxt-tag-team-debuts-at-aew-full-gear/">Former WWE/NXT tag team debuts at AEW Full Gear</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Former WWE tag team and one time NXT tag team champions, the Creed Brothers under their real names of Jacob and Drew Kasper and now known as the Kasper Brothers, made their debut at Saturday&#8217;s AEW Full Gear, at the Mortgage Matchup Center in Phoenix, Arizona.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Below is an excerpt from <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397439-aew-full-gear-results-11-14-26-anarchy-in-the-arena-title-matches-and-more/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Alex Kahrs&#8217; AEW Full Gear recap</a> of the debut!</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Bucks are presented with their titles, but don’t get long to celebrate as the Motor City Machine Guns come out to confront…or rather congratulate the champions. They help the Bucks up and shake hands, reminding the champs they are coming after them…when we get a siren throughout the arena. This is followed by some music for a pair of new arrivals in the <strong>Kasper Brothers</strong>…who turn out to be the men formerly known as the Creeds!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">They come down to the ring and immediately go after the Bucks and MCMG…until FTR make their way out for the save! …or maybe not brother, because they join the Guns in beating down the other two teams in the ring. This ends with the Kaspers and FTR shaking hands before leaving the ring.</p>
</blockquote>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="zxx" dir="ltr"><a href="https://t.co/ihypi9fK6N">https://t.co/ihypi9fK6N</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2121793626288353546?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 15, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After their debut, Tony Khan took to social media to announce the Kasper Brothers are officially All Elite!</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="777" height="756" src="https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/image-2.png" alt="" class="wp-image-397556" srcset="https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/image-2.png 777w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/image-2-600x584.png 600w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/image-2-550x535.png 550w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/image-2-379x369.png 379w" sizes="(max-width: 777px) 100vw, 777px" /></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">It was <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/396686-tag-team-departs-wwe/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">reported back on November 6</a>, the Creed Brothers departed WWE after their contracts expired. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Brutus Creed first signed with WWE back in 2020. Julius signed a contract a year later. After several years in NXT, the team was moved to Raw in 2023. For a period of time they were put with Chad Gable as part of the American Made heel faction.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397497-former-wwe-nxt-tag-team-debuts-at-aew-full-gear/">Former WWE/NXT tag team debuts at AEW Full Gear</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397497-former-wwe-nxt-tag-team-debuts-at-aew-full-gear/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Ratings reports for AEW Full Gear &#8216;go-home&#8217; edition of Dynamite and Collision</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397450-ratings-reports-for-aew-full-gear-go-home-edition-of-dynamite-and-collision/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397450-ratings-reports-for-aew-full-gear-go-home-edition-of-dynamite-and-collision/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:14:38 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[11/11/26 AEW Collision ratings]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[11/11/26 AEW Dynamite ratings]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397450</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Wrestlenomics has confirmed the viewership and ratings reports for the special &#8220;3-hour&#8221; edition of AEW Dynamite and Collision&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397450-ratings-reports-for-aew-full-gear-go-home-edition-of-dynamite-and-collision/">Ratings reports for AEW Full Gear &#8216;go-home&#8217; edition of Dynamite and Collision</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Wrestlenomics has confirmed the viewership and ratings reports for the special &#8220;3-hour&#8221; edition of AEW <a href="https://wrestlenomics.com/articles/2026/aew-dynamite-nov-11-on-tbs-742000-viewers-0-16-p18-49-rating-tv-ratings-analysis/">Dynamite</a> and <a href="https://wrestlenomics.com/articles/2026/aew-collision-nov-11-on-tbs-500000-viewers-0-12-p18-49-rating-tv-ratings-analysis/">Collision</a> on 11/11, which served as a &#8220;go-home&#8221; for Full Gear.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Dynamite drew 742,000 viewers on TBS, scoring a 0.16 rating in the key demo for a show that ultimately had a 27-minute overrun.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This is down from the previous week, which saw the show draw 792,000 viewers and score a 0.24 rating.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The special edition of Collision that immediately followed drew 500,000 viewers on TBS, scoring a 0.12 rating in the key demo for a show that had a 9-minute overrun.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This is up from the previous week&#8217;s show, which drew 376,000 viewers on TNT and scored a 0.08 rating in the key demo in its usual Saturday night timeslot.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397450-ratings-reports-for-aew-full-gear-go-home-edition-of-dynamite-and-collision/">Ratings reports for AEW Full Gear &#8216;go-home&#8217; edition of Dynamite and Collision</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397450-ratings-reports-for-aew-full-gear-go-home-edition-of-dynamite-and-collision/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>AEW to announce Continental Classic competitors during MNF halftime</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397446-aew-to-announce-continental-classic-competitors-during-mnf-halftime/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397446-aew-to-announce-continental-classic-competitors-during-mnf-halftime/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:17:20 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Continental Classic]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[halftime]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Jon Moxley]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Monday Night Football]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Tony Khan]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397446</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Tony Khan revealed on social media that participants for this year&#8217;s AEW Continental Classic will be announced on&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397446-aew-to-announce-continental-classic-competitors-during-mnf-halftime/">AEW to announce Continental Classic competitors during MNF halftime</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Tony Khan revealed on social media that participants for this year&#8217;s AEW Continental Classic will be announced on the company&#8217;s social media at halftime during Monday Night Football.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The NFL game will see the Baltimore Ravens face the Los Angeles Chargers with a kickoff of 8:15 p.m. Eastern.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Of this year&#8217;s Continental Classic participants, Jon Moxley is the only one already confirmed with his status as the reigning AEW Continental Champion.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The tournament will begin on the 11/18 edition of Dynamite.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="zxx" dir="ltr"><a href="https://t.co/lbIv1UM7WV">https://t.co/lbIv1UM7WV</a></p>&mdash; Tony Khan (@TonyKhan) <a href="https://x.com/TonyKhan/status/2121724857469841706?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 14, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397446-aew-to-announce-continental-classic-competitors-during-mnf-halftime/">AEW to announce Continental Classic competitors during MNF halftime</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397446-aew-to-announce-continental-classic-competitors-during-mnf-halftime/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Report: Update on TNA Destination X main event</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397443-report-update-on-tna-destination-x-main-event/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397443-report-update-on-tna-destination-x-main-event/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:57:06 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Impact Wrestling News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[card subject to change]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Destination X]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[main event]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[TNA]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397443</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>PWInsider has reported that a change is likely coming to the main event of TNA Wrestling&#8217;s upcoming Destination&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397443-report-update-on-tna-destination-x-main-event/">Report: Update on TNA Destination X main event</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://www.pwinsider.com/article/213687/tna-destination-x-main-event-will-change.html?p=1">PWInsider</a> has reported that a change is likely coming to the main event of TNA Wrestling&#8217;s upcoming Destination X pay-per-view in the midst of widespread flight issues.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">With the FAA implementing a ground stop on November 13, a number of flights were postponed or outright canceled.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Among those dealing with the travel issues is Trey Miguel, who is slated to challenge Leon Slater for the TNA World Championship.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The report notes that &#8220;unless there&#8217;s some sort of miracle&#8221; Miguel will not make the show, as TNA creative is taking stock of who is arriving at Edmonton in time for the show.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TNA President Carlos Silva confirmed there would be changes made to the show due to these travel issues, though no further details were given as of this writing.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">The show must &#8211; and will &#8211; go on!<br><br>TNA Wrestling confirmed that Destination X is still set for Sunday, November 15, at the Edmonton EXPO Centre, despite numerous travel issues resulting from the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) nationwide ground stop across the United States… <a href="https://t.co/5VZse61M9i">pic.twitter.com/5VZse61M9i</a></p>&mdash; TNA Wrestling (@ThisIsTNA) <a href="https://x.com/ThisIsTNA/status/2121674901064978860?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 14, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397443-report-update-on-tna-destination-x-main-event/">Report: Update on TNA Destination X main event</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397443-report-update-on-tna-destination-x-main-event/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>AEW Full Gear Results – 11/14/26 (Anarchy in the Arena, title matches, and more!)</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397439-aew-full-gear-results-11-14-26-anarchy-in-the-arena-title-matches-and-more/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397439-aew-full-gear-results-11-14-26-anarchy-in-the-arena-title-matches-and-more/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW Full Gear Results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[11/14/26 AEW Full Gear results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[3-Way Match]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW International Championship]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW National Championship]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW Women's World Championship]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW Women's World Tag Team Championship]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW World Championship]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW World Tag Team Championship]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW World Trios Championship]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Anarchy in the Arena]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[TBS Championship]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Texas Death Match]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397439</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>AEW Full Gear ResultsNovember 14, 2026Phoenix, Arizona (Mortgage Matchup Center)Results by: Alex Kahrs of Wrestleview.com Full Gear Buy&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397439-aew-full-gear-results-11-14-26-anarchy-in-the-arena-title-matches-and-more/">AEW Full Gear Results – 11/14/26 (Anarchy in the Arena, title matches, and more!)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>AEW Full Gear Results</strong><br><strong>November 14, 2026</strong><br><strong>Phoenix, Arizona (Mortgage Matchup Center)</strong><br><strong>Results by: Alex Kahrs of Wrestleview.com</strong></p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full is-resized"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="675" src="https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/mmcenter.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-397440" style="width:322px;height:auto" srcset="https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/mmcenter.jpg 1200w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/mmcenter-600x338.jpg 600w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/mmcenter-380x214.jpg 380w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/mmcenter-550x309.jpg 550w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/mmcenter-800x450.jpg 800w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/mmcenter-1160x653.jpg 1160w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></figure>



<h3 id="full-gear-buy-in-panel-discussion-and-more-airing-on-aews-youtube-and-social-media-channels" class="wp-block-heading">Full Gear Buy In (Panel Discussion and More) &#8211; Airing on AEW&#8217;s YouTube and social media channels:</h3>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-4-3 wp-has-aspect-ratio"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<iframe loading="lazy" title="AEW Full Gear Buy In LIVE TONIGHT - 11/14 | 7pm ET / 6pm CT / 4pm PT" width="1200" height="675" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/0lAcHGwYW0w?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
</div></figure>



<h3 id="full-gear-tailgate-brawl-airing-on-tnt-and-hbo-max" class="wp-block-heading">Full Gear Tailgate Brawl &#8211; Airing on TNT and HBO Max:</h3>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Jungle Jack Perry def. &#8220;The Beast&#8221; Mortos</li>



<li>Don Callis Family (Wardlow, El Clon, and &#8220;The Jet&#8221; Kevin Knight) def. Jaden Monroe, RJ Wylde, and Jordan Cruz</li>



<li><strong>8-Man Tag:</strong> Boom &amp; Doom and SkyFlight (Darius Martin and Matt Sydal) def. Don Callis Family (RPG Vice, Lance Archer, and Josh Alexander)</li>



<li><strong>TBS Championship 4-Way Match:</strong> Queen Aminata (c) def. Persephone, Skye Blue, and Hyan</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">With that, it&#8217;s time to gear up for AEW Full Gear&#8217;s main card!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We open with a video package hyping up the main feuds leading into tonight&#8217;s show, before heading to ringside for our opening contest. From there we get a video package for this &#8220;dream match&#8221; as Adam Copeland challenges Kazuchika Okada for the AEW International Championship at Full Gear!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back at ringside, Cope makes his entrance to a massive pop from the Phoenix crowd, who sings Adam&#8217;s theme as he makes his way toward the ring. Out next is the champion as Kazuchika Okada makes his entrance, also getting a good pop from the crowd as he enters the ring to get things underway!</p>



<h3 id="aew-international-championship-kazuchika-okada-c-vs-adam-copeland" class="wp-block-heading">AEW International Championship: Kazuchika Okada (c) vs. Adam Copeland</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Big &#8220;AEW&#8221; chant as the bell rings, with both men staring each other down. The crowd is thrilled for this match, which seems to almost overshadow anything actually happening until the two lock up. Okada takes Cope to the ropes, but the challenger breaks free as the crowd chants &#8220;f&#8211;k Don Callis.&#8221; Exchange of waist locks between both men before they change to another tie up, which ends with Okada getting Adam to the ropes again. Clean break is not so clean as he knees Cope in the gut, but Adam responds with a leg lariat before ducking a Rainmaker lariat&#8230;only for Okada to roll out of the way of a spear attempt!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Okada takes a breather on the outside as the ref begins the count, which gets broken as Okada dips into the ring for just a moment before leaving again. Cope goes after the champ, which costs him as he gets sent into the ring steps by the Rainmaker instead. Okada pulls off some of the protective padding from the floor before dipping into the ring to break the ref&#8217;s count again, and then goes for a tombstone piledriver&#8230;only for the challenger to counter with a body slam to the padded flooring instead.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He sets up a chair to seat Okada upon for a couple shots, including a boot to the face sending the champ to the floor. He picks up Okada, sending him into the barricade multiple times before bringing him back into the ring. Okada quickly manages to roll back out of the ring, but as he climbs onto the apron he gets knocked back down with a knee from the Rated R Superstar&#8230;who scares off Callis at ringside, only to take a dropkick into the barricade by the Rainmaker!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Okada once again breaks the ref&#8217;s count before attacking the challenger some more, with Callis shouting that Cope&#8217;s career ends tonight. Okada gives Don a hug before bringing Cope back into the ring. He mocks Adam with a boot to the head, following up with a neckbreaker to keep the challenger down.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Copeland gets back to his feet, but not for long as Okada takes him back down to the canvas. He watches the challenger try to get back up, smiling after taking him down hard with another DDT. He lands another hard shot on Cope for the cover, but Adam manages to grab the bottom rope to force a break. Cope back on his feet to trade shots, but he takes a boot from the Rainmaker.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Okada hits a scoop slam on the challenger, followed by an elbow drop. He favors his arm but manages to have enough strength to flip the crowd off. Cope stops a Rainmaker lariat before sending the champ down to the mat. He looks for a spear from the corner, but takes a neckbreaker on the knee of Okada instead.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The champ heads out of the ring, grabbing his title to inflict more damage, but the ref stops him before Cope stacks Okada up for a close two count! Both men down as the ref begins a standing count. They manage to get to their feet before charging at each other with a big boot&#8230;which ends with a double down of sorts instead, and the ref begins a new count.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The two fight to their feet until Okada catches Cope with a dropkick, but the challenger ducks a Rainmaker to take the champ down&#8230;only for Okada to send him to the ropes, getting the opening he needs for a tombstone piledriver! Cope slowly gets to his feet as the champ looks to take him out with his own move&#8230;but Adam catches Okada with an uppercut instead!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Copeland back on his feet as he gives Okada a taste of his own medicine to flip him off. He goes to the corner for a spear, but Okada gets out of harm&#8217;s way. Callis catches Cope by the ankle, and as the ref admonishes him for this Cope goes for a spear on the champ&#8230;running shoulder first into the title instead! Okada follows up with an Impaler DDT, sending the challenger down to the exposed concrete floor.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The ref begins a count as Okada starts to bring Cope to his feet, only to let him stay down as he returns to the ring. The count reaches seven when Okada decides to bring his opponent back into the ring. Okada is smiling as the ref may be looking to call the match off. Instead, Okada goes for the cover&#8230;only to pull Cope back up from the mat. He does this again, before bringing Cope to his feet for a Rainmaker lariat to secure the win and retain his title.</p>



<h3 id="winner-via-pinfall-and-still-aew-international-champion-kazuchika-okada" class="wp-block-heading">Winner via pinfall and still AEW International Champion: Kazuchika Okada</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We get a replay of the finish as Okada celebrates his victory outside the ring and up the ramp. The ref checks on Copeland as Okada poses with his title on the stage. The crowd starts to cheer for Cope&#8217;s efforts tonight when Okada runs back into the ring to go after him again. Cope breaks away from a Rainmaker attempt as Okada escapes up the ramp, the ref shouting at him that he&#8217;s already won the match.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">With that we get a video package hyping up our next match, as Davis and Doyle challenge The Young Bucks for the AEW World Tag Team Championship at Full Gear!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fresh off a dominant Title Eliminator victory to earn this shot, Davis and Doyle make their entrance at ringside. Out next are the champs as The Young Bucks make their way to the ring to get things underway!</p>



<h3 id="aew-world-tag-team-championship-the-young-bucks-c-vs-davis-doyle" class="wp-block-heading">AEW World Tag Team Championship: The Young Bucks (c) vs. Davis &amp; Doyle</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We start things off with Matt and Doyle, as Davis distracts Matt enough for a beatdown by Doyle. Doyle brings in Nick as the challengers continue to inflict the pain they gave the Bucks weeks ago. Doyle sends Nick over the barricade into the timekeeper&#8217;s area while Davis sends Matt back into the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Matt fights off a double team by the pair as Nick makes his way back to the ring. Davis gets a tag as he goes after Matt, but Nick makes a blind tag to bring the champs back into things&#8230;until Jake levels them both with a clothesline! Davis sends Nick to the ropes before tagging in Doyle, and the pair lay out Nick before mocking the crowd. Nick sent to the corner, keeping Jake off his game as Matt gets the tag.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Double-team by the Bucks sends Doyle off his feet, before sending Davis to the outside when he tries to come in. He pulls them to the outside, but both challengers are fended off by the Bucks until a dive attempt leads to a double forearm by Davis and Doyle&#8230;who send the Bucks crashing into each other!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Matt brought back into the ring as Davis tags in. The challengers pummel him with forearms before dropping him to the canvas, and Davis gets a nearfall as a result. Davis drops Matt again as Doyle sends Nick off the apron, and a tag allows Doyle to get a two count on Matt before tagging Dunkzilla back in. Sitout senton by Davis, who gets a two count before Matt kicks out. Matt fights out of the corner for a roll up, but Davis breaks it up as Doyle then stops him from going for a tag.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Matt goes for a sunset flip, which connects with an assist from Nick for a two count broken up by Doyle. Tag made between Davis and Doyle as they continue to keep Matt away from the corner. Doyle with a bearhug on Matt, going after the previously injured lower back. Matt boxes Doyle&#8217;s ears to break free, but is sent to the corner where he knocks Davis off the apron. He goes for a seated senton off the apron but is caught by Davis, who ends up getting taken out by Nick instead!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back in the ring, Matt fakes out Doyle by calling for a superkick only to drop him with a DDT&#8230;and manages to make the tag to Nick! Nick sends Jake to the corner for a flurry of offense before being shoved away by Doyle. Double-team kick in the corner keeps Doyle off his game, before Nick charges at Davis with a dive to the outside. With Davis down, Doyle is caught with a cross body for a two count. Davis ends up crashing onto Doyle when he goes to stop a subsequent pin attempt.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">All four men are in the ring now as the Bucks manage to sweep the challengers off their feet. They go up top for a double team, but the slow movement allows Davis and Doyle to stop the champs. Both teams go at it on opposite corners until the Bucks take over with a pair of sunset flips. Senton and elbow drop connect, but the Bucks only get a two count with Doyle officially kicking out.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Matt with a tag as they send the challengers to the outside for a dive, only to be cut off by Davis and Doyle. Matt is brought back into the ring as Doyle lands a powerbomb, and Davis follows up with a Rolling Thunder suplex. Cover by Doyle but it&#8217;s only good for two as Nick breaks it up&#8230;before sending Davis to the outside and to the floor with a DDT!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Bucks land a series of superkicks on Doyle in the ring, but a BTE Trigger gets barely a two count before Doyle shoves Matt out of the ring to break the pin. They go for another double superkick but get caught with a double powerbomb by Doyle instead. Tag made to Davis&#8230;who runs into a double superkick by the champs! Davis fights back to send Matt to the canvas before attacking both Bucks on the ropes&#8230;followed by a double piledriver, but that is not quite enough to keep the champs down for three.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Tag made as the challengers look to take out Matt&#8230;only for Nick to intercept Davis and send Doyle off the turnbuckle with a German suplex. Bucks with the BTE Trigger on Davis and Doyle, but both men kick out at two to emphasize they&#8217;re still in this match!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Matt looks to pick Davis up for a TK Driver, but needs some help with that from Nick&#8230;who then gets stopped at the apron by Doyle. Doyle sends Nick crashing into the timekeeper area as Davis drops Matt with a pendulum piledriver&#8230;only for Matt to narrowly kick out at two! Doyle with the tag as the challengers go to the corners for a double lariat, but Matt sends Davis out of the ring&#8230;and Dunkzilla is kept out by Nick as Matt rolls up Doyle long enough for the win!</p>



<h3 id="winners-via-pinfall-and-still-aew-world-tag-team-champions-the-young-bucks" class="wp-block-heading">Winners via pinfall and still AEW World Tag Team Champions: The Young Bucks</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Bucks are presented with their titles, but don&#8217;t get long to celebrate as the Motor City Machine Guns come out to confront&#8230;or rather congratulate the champions. They help the Bucks up and shake hands, reminding the champs they are coming after them&#8230;when we get a siren throughout the arena. This is followed by some music for a pair of new arrivals in the <strong>Kasper Brothers</strong>&#8230;who turn out to be the men formerly known as the Creeds!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">They come down to the ring and immediately go after the Bucks and MCMG&#8230;until FTR make their way out for the save! &#8230;or maybe not brother, because they join the Guns in beating down the other two teams in the ring. This ends with the Kaspers and FTR shaking hands before leaving the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We go to a video package for our next match, as Hangman Adam Page and Brodido defend the AEW World Trios Championship against Swerve Strickland and The New Level in a Texas Death Match!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back at ringside, Strickland and New Level make their entrances first as we get a glimpse at the weapons around the ring. We get a video from the &#8220;Swerve House&#8221; (Silver Dollar) Saloon as Brody King tries to get a Shirley Temple, only to be told to leave. This leads to King getting in a fight with nearly all the men in the saloon, with Hangman Adam Page waiting outside to take out any stragglers. They are joined by Bandido as they ride off into the proverbial sunset on horses to take us back to ringside.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The champs make their way out as commentary talks about the new championship belts themselves, which have small tributes to the late PAC, and with all six men here we get things underway! (A quick note on the rules of this match: simultaneous knockouts OR one man surrendering is the only way to end this match!)</p>



<h3 id="aew-world-trios-championship-texas-death-match-hangman-adam-page-brodido-c-vs-swerve-strickland-the-new-level" class="wp-block-heading">AEW World Trios Championship &#8211; Texas Death Match: Hangman Adam Page &amp; Brodido (c) vs. Swerve Strickland &amp; The New Level</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">All six men go at it in the ring until we&#8217;re left with Swerve and Bandido in the ring. Bandido hits a 21 Plex on Swerve before going after the New Level on the outside, while Brody grabs wooden skewers from otuside the ring. The champs set up their opponents on the apron&#8230;before driving the skewers into each man&#8217;s forehead! All three challengers drop to the floor as the champs celebrate in the ring. They go for a dive to the outside, but run into steel chairs to the face! Kofi and Creed in particular are panicking over the sight of the skewers in their heads as Nana helps remove them.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Creed goes after Brody, setting him up on a chair for a hip attack that drives King into the barricade. He starts mocking Brody, who drops Austin to the floor. We see Creed reach under the ring apron as King goes after him&#8230;only to be hit with a trombone wrapped with barbed wire! He plays some tunes before attacking Brody with the instrument again, and then goes to work dealing with the barbed wire on a table before Page goes after him. Meanwhile, Kofi aids Strickland in going after Bandido.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Page grabs some of the cut-off wire and starts to wrap it around his arm when Kofi cuts him off with a kick, bringing him back into the ring. He goes to the ropes but takes a clothesline courtesty of a barbed wire arm from Hangman, who takes out Swerve with it as well.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He starts to wrap the barbed wire around the mouth of Kofi when Creed stops him&#8230;and this leads to Creed getting the same treatment, until Swerve slams a chair against Hangman&#8217;s back! Bandido comes in with a dropkick, driving that chair into the face of Strickland&#8230;but Swerve responds by attacking the ROH World Champion with the chair. Swerve is busted open as he props the chair up on the mat, bringing Bandido to the turnbuckle. The luchador fights back with a kick as Brody brings some more chairs into the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">King sets up a bed of chairs as Bandido and Swerve fight it out on the turnbuckle, with the luchador sending Strickland into the chairs with a DDT before New Level get back into the ring. The pair take down Bandido before attacking Brody, who fights back before bringing one of the barbed wire tables into the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He props it against the corner and ends up sending Creed into that corner&#8230;only for Austin to dodge a cannonball senton, forcing Brody to get wrapped up in the barbed wire as he leaves the ring with the table broken in half. New Level pull the broken table out before setting that and pieces of the trombone over the body of Brody. They keep Bandido down before Creed gives a shoutout to Cactus Jack with an elbow drop off the apron. We see Hangman back in the ring now, but so too is Swerve Strickland&#8230;and each man has a staple gun in his hand as they circle the mat.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">They set up a pair of chairs in the center of the ring and have what I can best describe as a &#8220;staple off&#8221; as they shoot staples into each other&#8217;s chests. Bandido comes in to intervene and takes a staple before Swerve gets knocked down by Page. He goes to the apron but is stopped by Nana, before dropping the Prince to the floor..which gives Swerve an opening to take Hangman out!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In comes Brody King, who reveals a glove covered in thumbtacks&#8230;that he uses for a chop to the chest of Strickland! Creed comes after him but takes an Iron Claw with the glove by King, who lays him out with a right hand. Brody leaves the ring to grab a bag from under the ring, revealing a pile of even more thumbtacks that is spilled onto the canvas. He goes after Creed, who fights back before landing a fisherman&#8217;s buster sending King onto the tacks! Creed fires up as he hits a tope onto Bandido and Page over and over.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This ends with Creed sending Bandido into the ring steps before going back into the ring one more time. Prince Nana has another bag in his hand. Creed pulls something out of the bag&#8230;and it&#8217;s a Power Glove! Creed really is playing with power, and we&#8217;re about to find out how true that is as he hits a Dragon Punch on King&#8230;and it explodes in Brody&#8217;s face to knock him down to the mat!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">With all three champs down the ref begins the count&#8230;but Bandido manages to get up to stop it! Page is back up as well as Kofi and Swerve try to deal with them. Creed comes out of the ring to help as Page gets knocked away, bringing Bandido near an oil well to summon fire that gets dangerously close to the luchador&#8217;s face! He does it a second time for good measure, but Page fights back with a light tube on Kofi and a Dead Eye on Creed.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He goes back to the ring to go after Swerve and help Brody, but New Level are back on their feet and head to the ring. They prop Page up on some chairs, possibly trying to keep him tied down as they find a window pane to set on top of Hangman. Kofi steps onto the barricade and hits a double leg drop, breaking the glass over Page&#8217;s body to send him back down to the floor!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Creed brings another barbed wire table into the ring, but they are distracted by Bandido trying to make the save. Strickland brings out some padlocks on chains&#8230;and they level King with one of them before placing a lock in his mouth for a T.I.P. by Kofi! Brody is left laying as the challengers go after Bandido in the ring. Page comes in for the save but is quickly fought off before New Level set up Bandido for a House Call by Swerve&#8230;only for King to run into the ring to take the proverbial bullet!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The challengers go for it again, but Bandido starts to fight back. He catches a hurricanrana from Kofi, driving him through the table with a powerbomb instead&#8230;but Swerve catches him by surprise, before getting a chain from Nana. He starts to wrap it around the throat of the luchador, who pulls him to the mat instead. He goes to the opposite corner, climbing up top for a frog splash that sends Strickland into the tack pile.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Now it&#8217;s Bandido who has the chain, wrapping it around Swerve&#8217;s throat before sending him to the apron. Strickland manages to fight back and starts pulling apart Bandido&#8217;s mask to big boos from the crowd&#8230;until Page runs in for the save! Swerve narrowly avoids getting leveled by a steel chair, and draws blood from the Hangman which he seems to take great delight in as he, uh&#8230;lets some of it into his mouth. Ugh.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Page grabs the chair and fights off New Level, but hesitates when he sees Swerve&#8217;s bloody grin&#8230;only for Strickland to spit Page&#8217;s own blood back in his face! Swerve leaves the ring to grab a cinder block, recalling his previous Texas Death Match against the Hangman as he looks for Big Pressure on Page&#8230;but Bandido stops him with a kick to the back of the head.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Bandido follows up with an X-Knee to Swerve&#8217;s face before moving the cinder block to the middle of the ring. He looks for a 21 Plex to drive Strickland into it, but New Level stop it before dropping him with what looks like the Big Ending onto the edge of the block instead! Brody King comes running in, bringing New Level to the outside before propping barbed wire table pieces over them for a barricade cross body&#8230;only to take a Vertebreaker by Strickland onto the ring steps!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Swerve gets back into the ring, but Page is there as well as he takes out the challenger with a Buckshot Lariat&#8230;but a second one is stopped with a chair shot by Strickland! All six men are down as the ref begins the count. It gets to eight as Swerve manages to get to his feet, and right after the count of nine Page is only up enough to take a House Call that knocks him out for the final count! We have new trios champions!</p>



<h3 id="winners-via-knockout-and-new-aew-world-trios-champions-swerve-strickland-the-new-level" class="wp-block-heading">Winners via knockout and new AEW World Trios Champions: Swerve Strickland &amp; The New Level</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We get a replay of the big moments of this match as the new champions celebrate up the ramp and on the stage. We go backstage to see Don Callis talking to Kyle Fletcher and Ospreay gets a quick sparring session with Speedball ahead of defending the World Championship.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Commentary talks about Perry taking out Mortos with a muscle buster during the Tailgate Brawl, and the fact Samoa Joe could not make it to the show due to travel issues&#8230;but we do get a message FROM Samoa Joe, who has managed to find out what Perry did earlier. He addresses beating Jack in France and how that wasn&#8217;t enough for Perry to back away. Jack won&#8217;t worry about shaking Joe&#8217;s hand, when he is left shaking because of the Coquina Clutch in the middle of the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We get a video package hyping up the AEW Women&#8217;s World Tag Team Championship match up next, as Wrathlander challenge the Brawling Birds!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back at ringside, we get a video of Wrathlander discussing their first PPV entrance as a team. They come up with ideas before they&#8217;re interrupted by Billy Gunn, who they tell off before Tony Khan appears to tell them the video package is over and it&#8217;s time to go. Wrathlander tell each other &#8220;let&#8217;s f&#8211;king go&#8221; before we head back to ringside for the arrival of the challengers to a big pop from the crowd. The Brawling Birds also get a good reception on their way to the ring, before we get things underway!</p>



<h3 id="aew-womens-world-tag-team-championship-the-brawling-birds-c-vs-wrathlander" class="wp-block-heading">AEW Women&#8217;s World Tag Team Championship: The Brawling Birds (c) vs. Wrathlander</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We start off with Statlander and Windsor as they fight to the corner. They break free before trading shots, with Windsor blocking a Stat shoulder tackle before landing an elbow strike. She hits the ring but is dropped as Kris connects with a shoulder tackle this time. Windsor fights back from her feet for a tag to Hayter and drops Cameron from the apron as Jamie rolls Kris up for two.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Stat starts to fight back before making a tag to Harley for a double-team, which gets Cameron a nearfall. Tag to Windsor as Harley does the splits to avoid a clothesline. Blind tag by Stat as Harley takes Alex to the mat with a headscissors. She keeps Windsor down for a kick by Kris, who takes her to the floor outside while Harley brings down Hayter. Jamie fights back with a suplex on Cameron before taking out Stat once more, while Windsor drops Cameron back to the floor.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ref&#8217;s count is broken when Windsor brings Statlander back in the ring for a nearfall. Tag made to Hayer as the champs double-team Stat, but there is a slight mixup when Windsor starts to go for the cover. That allows Stat to kick out at two when Hayter makes the cover instead. Tag made to Cameron, who dodges the attack of Windsor for a thrust kick.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Brawling Birds fight back with a double-team allowing Jamie to get a two count. Harley starts to fight back before Hayter knocks Stat off the apron, and a tag is made to Windsor who fires off some shots on Cameron for a nearfall. Harley tries to fight back, eventually catching Windsor with a back suplex before tagging in Statlander. Hayter tags in as well and they trade offense, with Stat landing a Michinoku Driver for two.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Things break down as all four women go at it, with Harley landing some hard kicks on Hayter only to get laid out by Windsor&#8230;who gets leveled with a clothesline by Statlander! Hate Breaker on Cameron and the Birds have both challengers down as Jamie gets a two count.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Hayter and Harley go at it off a tag, until Stat gives an assist for a crucifix pin by Harley. Windsor breaks it up just in time and all four women are down. Stat is back up, but gets sent to the outside by the champs as they go after Cameron&#8230;but Kris is back in, and gets Windsor on her shoulders. This leads to a chicken fight between Cameron and Windsor until the latter drops Statlander with a reverse rana.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Harley and Jamie are left to trade shots on each other in the ring, with Harley landing a roundhouse kick. Hayter fires back with one of her own, but a Hayterade is blocked with a drop toe hold and a half crab&#8230;until Windsor breaks it up! A pair of lariats from Hayter and she goes for the cover&#8230;but Kris breaks it up!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Stat with the tag now but she gets set up for Two Birds One Stone&#8230;only for Harley to stop Hayter, pulling her out of the ring as Stat drops Windsor to the canvas for the pin and the win!</p>



<h3 id="winners-via-pinfall-and-new-aew-womens-world-tag-team-champions-wrathlander" class="wp-block-heading">Winners via pinfall and new AEW Women&#8217;s World Tag Team Champions: Wrathlander</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The now-former champs eventually shake hands with the better women on this night, and Wrathlander leave the ring to celebrate up the ramp. The win makes Kris Statlander a triple crown winner and gives Harley Cameron the distinction of being the first two-time Women&#8217;s World Tag Team Champion.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We go to the video promoting AEW Thanksgiving Eve Dynamite and Thanksgiving Collision from Omaha, Nebraska before going to ringside for our next match, as a video package hypes us up for Tommaso Ciampa defending the AEW National Championship against Ilja Dragunov at Full Gear!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back at ringside, Dragunov makes his entrance first before the champion makes his way to the ring to get this match underway!</p>



<h3 id="aew-national-championship-tommaso-ciampa-c-vs-ilja-dragunov" class="wp-block-heading">AEW National Championship: Tommaso Ciampa (c) vs. Ilja Dragunov</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Chants from the crowd as the two men circle the mat before locking up. Ciampa is taken to the mat by Dragunov, but the champ (uh) breaks free to get to his feet. They go at it again, which ends with an armbar of sorts from Ilja. Ciampa finds a way out, and gets his foot on the rope to break a pin attempt.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Tommaso gets the challenger to the corner and is forced to make a break, which gives Dragunov an opening to strike back. This leads to the two trading shots back and forth, until Ciampa catches Ilja with a side headlock. Dragunov counters to take the champ down for some right hands, but Ciampa turns it around for some shots of his own. Both men back up but Dragunov takes Ciampa down hard for a nearfall.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The two grapple until Dragunov sends Ciampa flying with a modified Magistral, and then sends him to the outside with a knee strike. Ciampa reaches for the hood of the announce table to stop a German suplex by Dragunov, and the champ runs into the ring to build up speed for a knee strike sending Dragunov off the apron to the floor! Tommaso lets us know that Ciampa Rules before going after the challenger, sending him into the barricade and driving his boot into Ilja&#8217;s face.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Dragunov starts to fight back, propping the champ up against the table for some elbows&#8230;only to be sent face first onto it by Tommaso, who then slams him against the ring steps! He mocks the challenger by sitting on the apron, giving himself applause and a pat on the back before going after the arm of Dragunov. He brings Ilja back into the ring for some more damage, stomping away at the arm for good measure.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Top wristlock into an elbow driver on the challenger, and Ciampa follows up with some kicks to the ribs. He goes back after the arm, but Dragunov breaks free before sending the champ to the ropes for a chop. This hurts the already injured arm and Ilja drops to the mat, allowing Tommaso to go back to work on him.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ciampa then blocks a German suplex and dodges the challenger from the ropes, landing a knee strike. He goes for a second one with the kneepad down, but Dragunov clips him with his injured hand! Ilja tries to roll up the champ twice, each one getting a nearfall. He goes after the knee of Ciampa, who blocks a lariat only to take an enziguri by the challenger! He follows up with some headbutts and forearms followed by a senton.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ciampa starts to fight back, but takes a German suplex by Dragunov for two. Ciampa stops him from going for another one, but gets laid out with a clothesline instead. Ciampa takes a D-Bomb to the leg as Ilja pulls him to the corner, and it looks like Ciampa is struggling as he gets set up on the top turnbuckle by Dragunov.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Tommaso bites the challenger&#8217;s hand to fight him off before dropping him to the canvas with an avalanche Air Raid Crash&#8230;but it looks like it caused some more damage to his leg as well, as he struggles to capitalize. Both men eventually on their feet as they trade shots, only for Ciampa to send Ilja out of the ring. He attacks the challenger on the floor before sending him face first onto the ring steps&#8230;and then picks him up for an Air Raid Crash on the edge of the steps! He brings Dragunov back in the ring for a running knee and the cover&#8230;but the challenger kicks out at two!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The fight makes its way to the apron as they fight it out some more, with Dragunov winning the fight as he takes the champ onto the hardest part of the ring with a suplex&#8230;and follows with a D-Bomb off the apron onto Ciampa&#8217;s head on the floor! The ref begins the count as the challenger struggles to get Tommaso to his feet, and both men are back in the ring around eight.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Dragunov takes the champ to the top turnbuckle for some headbutts, followed by a superplex sending Ciampa crashing against the canvas. He goes for a D-Bomb, but Ciampa dodges it and connects with a Fujiwara armbar. Ciampa then transitions into a running knee, with Dragunov dodging a second one before taking it the third time around&#8230;but it&#8217;s only good for two as the challenger kicks out!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Tommaso quickly goes for another armbar, but Dragunov breaks free before connecting with not one but two more D-Bombs to pick up the win! That&#8217;s three title changes in a row, folks!</p>



<h3 id="winner-via-pinfall-and-new-aew-national-champion-ilja-dragunov" class="wp-block-heading">Winner via pinfall and new AEW National Champion: Ilja Dragunov</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ilja celebrates with the title as we see Tommaso Ciampa trying to figure out his next steps after losing the title so quickly. With that, we go to a video package hyping up the start of the Continental Classic this Wednesday on Dynamite, and then another package hyping up our next match as Marina Shafir challenge Mercedes Moné for the AEW Women&#8217;s World Championship!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back at ringside, Marina Shafir makes her entrance through the crowd to a big reaction from the Phoenix crowd&#8230;who give a similar reaction for the arrival of the champion as Mercedes Moné makes her way to the ring. We get introductions for the challenger and the champion (who noticeably gets more boos by this poitn) as we get this match underway!</p>



<h3 id="aew-womens-world-championship-mercedes-mone-c-vs-marina-shafir" class="wp-block-heading">AEW Women&#8217;s World Championship: Mercedes Moné (c) vs. Marina Shafir</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Moné tries to avoid Shafir at first before going for a waistlock, which gets countered into a takedown by Marina. She ties up the champion for a unique submission, largely just to show that she can do it before she breaks the hold to flex on Moné. Mercedes doesn&#8217;t take kindly to this as she goes on the attack, sending the challenger to the corner. Marina blocks a monkey flip and manages to stop a Statement Maker that comes after. A series of throws by the challenger, with Mercedes blocking the last of these before going for a Money Maker. Marina blocks it and twists the arm of Moné to fully break free.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Mercedes looks for a rear naked choke on Shafir, who sends the champ to the corner before breaking free&#8230;only for Moné to knock her down for a double stomp to the back! Moné goes to work on Marina in the corner now, taking her down to the mat before mocking Shafir. She puts Marina in a hammerlock before transitioning into an armbreaker shades of either Swerve Strickland or Penta, but a resulting pin is stopped at one as Marina kicks out. Mercedes back at it as she gets a nearfall before going for an armbar.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The grip is not fully in place before Marina breaks free, spinning the champ around with a throw to the mat. Shafir fires off some more shots including a spinal tap before going for the cover, but Moné kicks out at two. Moné goes after the challenger, but Marina twists her around for a nearfall as we get dueling chants of &#8220;She&#8217;s our Problem&#8221; and &#8220;CEO&#8221;&#8230;and Moné connects with a Meteora for a two count!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Mercedes shouts down at her challenger before landing a slap to the face&#8230;with Shafir firing back with a callback to her Death Rider pal Daniel Garcia with a dance to mock the champ! Moné goes for a headscissors into an armbar, but Marina keeps the grip from being in tight before flipping off the champ&#8230;and then stomping her bare foot into the face of Moné! This disgusts Mercedes as she goes back after Marina, catching her with a crossface before Shafir counters into a pin for a two count to break the hold.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Shafir goes for a Brutalizer in honor of PAC, but Moné rolls through for a nearfall of her own to break that submission. Statement Maker by Moné but Marina rolls through to break free, only to be trapped on the ropes as Mercedes drives her arm onto the middle rope. Marina goes to the floor as Mercedes only barely manages to get a dive on her challenger&#8230;who catches her with Mother&#8217;s Milk on the floor!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Moné taps out, but it doesn&#8217;t matter if it&#8217;s not in the ring. Shafir brings the champ back into the ring as we get dueling chants again, and Moné catches the challenger for a two count. She goes for a cross body but gets caught by Shafir, who headbutts her and then spins the champ around with a giant swing! Mercedes uses the ropes to get back up, only to be driven onto the apron by Shafir before falling to the floor.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Marina brings the champ back to the ring, only to be tripped up by Moné who hits a Meteora sending Shafir against the apron&#8230;only for the challenger to fight back with a body slam sending Moné onto the hardest part of the ring! The fight ends up back in the ring, where Moné connects with a double knee to the back followed by a Backstabber rolled through into a Statement Maker!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Chants of &#8220;don&#8217;t give up&#8221; (or Marina) ring out as Shafir struggles toward the ropes&#8230;before rolling up the champ for a nearfall that breaks the hold. Both women are on their feet as Mercedes fires off some shots, mocking the challenger throughout&#8230;until Shafir drops the CEO with a kick sending her to the canvas. Shafir looks for a Death Rider DDT, but Moné counters out into a Statement Maker&#8230;that she transitions into a Brutalizer! Shafir is fired up by this, breaking free and locking in a Brutalizer of her own on the champion&#8230;who rolls through for a pin, grabbing the bottom rope with her legs for leverage to steal a win and retain her title here tonight!</p>



<h3 id="winner-via-pinfall-and-still-aew-womens-world-champion-mercedes-mone" class="wp-block-heading">Winner via pinfall and still AEW Women&#8217;s World Champion: Mercedes Moné</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Moné escapes the ring and Shafir&#8217;s wrath to celebrate her win as we go backstage, where an irate Tommaso Ciampa reflects on his struggles to hold the titles he&#8217;s won since joining AEW. He makes a demand to be entered into the Continental Classic, knowing full well the challenge that will await him. He knows it means nothing to bring the Psycho Killer or the Psycho King into this, but we will be getting Tommaso Ciampa.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He says we don&#8217;t have to believe he can get it done, but that he would have to be killed to be stopped.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">With that, we go to a video package for AEW Worlds End on December 19. Back at ringside, commentary reveals that Worlds End will have the semifinal matches for the Continental Classic, breaking the tradition of the tournament ending at the PPV (but you had to believe that was possible when they scheduled that show for mid-December)&#8230;and then, we go to a video package hyping up Anarchy in the Arena!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We return to ringside as Justin Roberts lets us know that anything goes, and once the music hits, we&#8217;re in for some serious s&#8211;t for Anarchy in the Arena! Out first are The Cut with matching hats and jackets, looking like the band of outlaws they think they are as they head to the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Conglomeration make their entrance through the crowd as The Cut leave the ring to intercept them. The two groups start brawling as Jon Moxley&#8217;s old &#8220;Wild Thing&#8221; theme hits to a big pop, as the Death Riders join the fray to get this match(???) underway!</p>



<h3 id="anarchy-in-the-arena-the-cut-jay-white-david-finlay-clark-connors-ace-austin-colten-gunn-and-austin-gunn-vs-death-riders-jon-moxley-daniel-garcia-gabe-kidd-the-conglomeration" class="wp-block-heading">Anarchy in the Arena: The Cut (Jay White, David Finlay, Clark Connors, Ace Austin, Colten Gunn, and Austin Gunn) vs. Death Riders (Jon Moxley, Daniel Garcia, &amp; Gabe Kidd) &amp; The Conglomeration (Orange Cassidy, Kyle O&#8217;Reilly, &amp; Roderick Strong)</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We start out with absolute bedlam as all of these men go at it in the crowd, so much so that it&#8217;s hard to keep track of it all until they end up back in the ring. Moxley&#8217;s theme finally comes to an end as Garcia challenges Finlay to a potential dance off&#8230;leading to our SECOND song of the night as DMX&#8217;s &#8220;Party Up&#8221; rings through the arena! This just gets crazier and crazier as the Riders regain control of the bout, laying out The Cut as we see Mox and Cassidy attack White and Finlay with forks in the corners.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Connors interrupts things before Austin pulls out a spoon, which only gets him attacked by Mox as the brawl continues. We see Cassidy chatting with a young fan in the front row as back in the ring, Austin Gunn and Ace Austin regain some control. Austin Gunn tries to regain some composure with his team as the Phoenix Suns mascot comes out with a drink bucket&#8230;revealing a fire extinguisher that he uses on Austin! Ace Austin goes after the mascot as Mox gets back into the fray.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We see glass spilled out of Cassidy&#8217;s backpack but to no avail as he gets attacked in the corner. Outside the ring, Colten Gunn goes after Mox only to be attacked with a skewer. In the ring, Cassidy gets dropped onto the pile of glass by Finlay not once but twice. White goes after Garcia outside the ring but Mox intervenes. Back in the ring, Cassidy sends Finlay onto the glass with a back body drop before Mox drags him along the glass. Bulldog choke by Mox but Connors and White break it up.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">O&#8217;Reilly goes after Connors on the outside as back in the ring, White goes after Kidd who comes back in. The music cuts off to boos from the crowd, as Jay goes back after Kidd with some barbed wire. Finlay starts to call him off, leading to an argument between Finlay and the Switchblade while Connors gets into the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We realize what&#8217;s happening as Finlay and Connors try to convince Gabe to rejoin his fellow Dogs in The Cut. It looks as though Kidd is considering it as he takes his PAC jersey off, as Connors and Finlay hand him a Cut shirt. He takes a chair as well, as Mox is propped up by Connors&#8230;only for Gabe to throw the chair into the face of Finlay! This leads to the music playing again as Mox takes out Finlay with a cutter.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cassidy gets into it as well before The Cut regain control after Finlay drops Strong with a backbreaker. This comes to an end with Mox and Cassidy locking in holds that are broken up by Ace Austin, and The Gunns lay out Orange only to be attacked by Kidd. Gabe drops Austin before taking out Colten in the corner&#8230;but he gets laid out with a glass bottle to the head by Connors! Strong drops Clark and then The Gunns get taken out with a double DDT by Cassidy.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Finlay gets dropped onto the glass as the music cuts again to more boos. Ace gets dropped onto a chair by Roddy, but Colten lays him out before Austin Gunn hits a Famouser sending Strong onto the chair. Jay White finally makes a cover off of all this, but Strong manages to kick out at two.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Jay White brings his branding iron into the ring, with Clark Connors heating it up&#8230;but in comes Marina to stop Jay! He drops the branding iron before being sent into the corner by Strong. He and Shair keep on the attack before staring each other down, remembering their battles against each other. The distraction is enough for Strong to be sent into Shafir by Austin, as Roddy is propped up for a branding&#8230;only for Wheeler Yuta to come running in for the save with a missile dropkick!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This leads to a rare chant in favor of Yuta as he joins the fight. He and Cassidy take down two of the Cut down before staring at each other due to their own beef&#8230;until STP comes out to get involved as well! They send Cassidy to the outside before sending Wheeler through a table&#8230;only to get dropped on by Cassidy!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back in the ring, Mox gets back in control before Mercedes Moné slides into the ring for a low blow. She talks down Moxley before the lights go out&#8230;and when they come back on, we see Kemonlito (a member of Death Riders through their CMLL excursion) in the ring! Moné goes after the micro wrestler, who fires back with a spinning headscissors that sends the CEO to the outside&#8230;where she gets laid out with a pounce by Willow Nightingale to a big pop.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Kemonlito doesn&#8217;t get time to celebrate this before being attacked by STP, who set him up on the apron for a sliding dropkick that sends him flying off to the floor&#8230;and then squishing him with a big splash from Shane Taylor himself! This is then interrupted by the arrival of Claudio in the parking lot. Austin Gunn looks ready as he leaves the ring with a trash can&#8230;only for the can to miss as Castagnoli drops him with an uppercut!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Infantry go after him but are taken out of the ring, with Connors and Ace being caught in a double giant swing of sorts from Claudio&#8217;s shoulders. He then goes after a returning Austin, who tries to attack him with a trash can&#8230;only to be sent into it with a giant swing, and then swung around with the can over him!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Jay goes for a Blade Runner on him but is fought off, only for STP to go after him. They set up a table before Claudio starts to go after them. It doesn&#8217;t last long before he&#8217;s propped over the table as Shane goes up top, but Claudio ends up sending Infantry out of the ring&#8230;before hoisting Taylor off the turnbuckle and through the table! Jay slides into the ring with a chair onto the back of Claudio, who is barely fazed. He takes another chair shot before sending White into the corner&#8230;leading to a train of attacks by the Death Riders and the Conglomeration that culminates in Kemonlito getting one over on the Switchblade!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Claudio gets the OK to launch him over to the outside to their opponents, and Garcia traps White with a Dragontamer into a stomp by Mox. Moxley goes for the cover but the Cut manage to break it up. We see Kidd fighting his old friends on the stage as back at ringside the Cut regain control with a 3:10 to Yuma sending (uh, someone?) through the table. Connors gets sent through the set, before Kidd brings him toward a table and pours out some alcochol over his head. Finlay fights him off and they end up setting the table on fire as back in the ring, Mox sends Colten out of the ring&#8230;only to be hit with a Blade Runner as Jay White picks up the win for his squad!</p>



<h3 id="winners-via-pinfall-the-cut" class="wp-block-heading">Winners via pinfall: The Cut</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The group returns to the ring, joining Switchblade in celebrating their win as their opponents are attended to. As this and cleanup goes on, we head backstage where Mick Foley talks to Adam Copeland. Foley asks as a friend what&#8217;s going on in Adam&#8217;s mind after his match tonight. Cope says he wanted tonight&#8217;s match to answer some questions&#8230;and it did. That&#8217;s all we get as we head back to ringside.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We see Nick Wayne up in a skybox, where he announces that Nick Wayne&#8230;is here at Full Gear. He talks about how after doing so much winmaxxing that he is now relaxing, so he is chillaxing&#8230;and why? Because Nick Wayne&#8230;beat Chris Jericho! Pyro goes off. His music starts to play, but he cuts it off to give us the news that Nick Wayne&#8230; beat Chris Jericho! Another shot of pyro for the Prodigy.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Commentary hypes up the upcoming Continental Classic, and I get clarification as they reveal that the semi-final and championship final take place at Worlds End on December 19. And with that, we go to a video package for our main event as Kyle Fletcher challenges his former friend Will Ospreay for the AEW World Championship at Full Gear!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back at ringside, a special entrance for Kyle Fletcher asks about destiny before the challenger makes his way out for this main event. We then get a video of Will Ospreay addressing his former friend ahead of their title match, before the champion makes his entrance to a massive pop. He poses for the fans once he&#8217;s in the ring, before we get introductions for the challenger and champion to get this main event underway!</p>



<h3 id="aew-world-championship-will-ospreay-c-vs-kyle-fletcher" class="wp-block-heading">AEW World Championship: Will Ospreay (c) vs. Kyle Fletcher</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Commentary makes note of the Don Callis Family and United Empire on either side of the ring as the bell sounds off, and the two men in the ring stare each other down to &#8220;AEW&#8221; chants. This leads to a pretty big &#8220;Protostar&#8221; chant, which surprises Kyle a little bit but doesn&#8217;t seem to faze Ospreay one bit.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We finally get contact as the two lock up, each looking for the advantage. This ends up on the ropes, where the ref calls for a break. Ospreay shoves Fletcher away before going after the arm of the challenger, but Kyle turns it around before being sent toward the ropes. The two trade offense until Kyle gets the champ to the corner, mocking Will before slapping him in the face.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">They lock up again, with Fletcher taking control. Ospreay counters out of it, and delivers a slap of his own to the face of the challenger. Kyle regroups in the corner, getting back up to his feet as he looks for a test of strength. Ospreay is hesitant to join in, but eventually does as they see who can get the upper hand. Fletcher twists the arms of the champ, who turns it around to a standstill.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fletcher regains control, getting the champ to the mat and on his shoulders for a one count. Ospreay breaks free but is caught with a shoulder tackle by the challenger, who then sends Ospreay to the ropes. Will counters with a hurricanrana and looks for a Hidden Blade&#8230;but Kyle absorbs it on the chest before knocking Ospreay down, forcing him to take a breather on the outside.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Champ with a side headlock as he takes Fletcher to the mat, but Kyle fights back to his feet. Dueling chants of &#8220;let&#8217;s go Ospreay&#8221; and &#8220;Protostar&#8221; as the two trade offense again, with Kyle getting dropped onto the rope as Will regains control of the match. Ospreay lands a chop on Fletcher in the corner, but Kyle fights back to go to the ropes&#8230;where Ospreay catches him with a kick forcing the challenger to leave the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ospreay goes for a dive, but gets caught by the Protostar before they take turns trying to send each other into the barricade. Ospreay wins this battle with a clothesline before both men head back to the ring. Kyle gets caught with a clothesline off the apron but then catches Ospreay coming down on him from the turnbuckle&#8230;sending him onto the hardest part of the ring with a nasty powerbomb!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Will is brought back into the ring as Fletcher goes to work on the champ some more. He sends Ospreay into the corner before slamming him to the mat for a two count. He attacks the champ&#8217;s head, mocking Windsor at ringside as he continues going after her husband. She checks on Ospreay while Fletcher waits for him to get back on his feet. Will is back up but wobbly as Kyle drops him with a body slam, holding onto the wrist.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fletcher starts mocking Andrade as he continues to work on the champ, who fires back with some shots before catching the challenger with a corkscrew kick off the ropes! Flying forearm connects, but only gets a two as Fletcher kicks out. Fletcher in the corner as Ospreay gets up, landing an inzayn running kick to the face before taking the challenger down hard to the mat.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fletcher gets back on his feet but takes a forearm to the midsection&#8230;only to fire back with a Michinoku Driver for a nearfall. Ospreay breaks out of a brainbuster attempt, but gets taken down anyway as the challenger follows up with a half and half suplex. Ospreay uses the ropes to get up, but takes a running kick by Fletcher that drops him back down. Kyle goes back to talking smack with El Idolo before looking for a half and half on the apron, but the champ fights back.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This leads to a back and forth, with Fletcher blocking an Oscutter only for the champ to look for a Styles Clash&#8230;sending Kyle down to the floor! Don Callis leaves commentary to check on his man as both men are down. The ref tells Callis to back off before returning to the ring, where he begins a count.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ospreay gets back in the ring around seven, with Fletcher making it just after nine&#8230;only to take a dropkick from the champ! Oscutter connects, but only gets a two as the Protostar kicks out just in time.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Will heads to the corner for a Hidden Blade, but the challenger is back up already. Back and forth they go with strikes. Ospreay wins out as he gets Fletcher on his shoulders for a Go to Sleepy Hollow, but as he goes to the ropes he gets caught with an Anti-Air from Fletcher&#8230;who follows up with a Liger Bomb for a close nearfall! With both men down, the ref begins a standing count.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fletcher is the first to his feet as he goes to the ropes, but Ospreay fires back with a flurry of offense&#8230;until Fletcher levels him with a lariat! Ospreay hits a Stundog Millionaire in retaliation before heading to the corner, where he takes another running kick followed by a brainbuster! Cover by the Protostar, but Will gets a shoulder up just in the nick of time.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The crowd didn&#8217;t seem to like that, chanting &#8220;ref you suck&#8221; as Fletcher starts firing back with a running kick to the back. He has Ospreay in his arms, and chooses to send the champ into the corner&#8230;allowing the champ to connect with an Oscutter for a two count!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Osprey goes to work on the challenger now, giving back a measure of what he&#8217;s had to take up to this point. He brings Kyle to the corner before the ref forces a break. Fletcher tries to charge at him, but takes a shot to the midsection&#8230;and as Kyle drops to the mat, the crowd is booing the champ!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fletcher is back on his feet for a thrust kick, garnering an &#8220;ooh&#8221; from the crowd as the two go back and forth on offense once more. Ospreay gets him back on his feet for an abdominal stretch, and Kyle starts to break free only to be trapped again as the crowd chants &#8220;let&#8217;s go Kyle&#8221; and &#8220;let&#8217;s go Will.&#8221; Ospreay transitions to a flying octopus hold, but Fletcher counters out to send the champ into the turnbuckle.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ospreay heads to the corner, where Kyle sets him up on the turnbuckle. Uppercut by Fletcher, but the champ fights out of it for a Cheeky Nando&#8217;s series of kicks to the face. Ospreay in the corner as he looks for a Hidden Blade&#8230;only to run into one by the challenger instead! Fletcher charges but takes a hurricanrana by Ospreay, who transitions into Styles Clash&#8230;but Fletcher kicks out. Hidden Blade connects as the champ goes for another cover&#8230;and the Protostar gets his shoulder up!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Callis goes to talk to Fletcher as Ospreay takes a look at the black arrows on the stage. He looks to honor the late PAC one more time, bringing Fletcher to the corner as he climbs up for a Black Arrow&#8230;but Fletcher intercepts him for a brainbuster sending him to the mat! Kyle makes the cover&#8230;and the champ just barely kicks out at two.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Duelling chants as Fletcher brings the champ back up. He looks for another turnbuckle brainbuster, pulling off the pad before the ref argues with him. Ospreay breaks free of the buster attempt this time, pulling Fletcher&#8217;s foot off the ropes which sends the challenger face first into the exposed turnbuckle before Will connects with another Hidden Blade.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fletcher slowly gets to his feet using the ropes, only to take a crescent kick by the champ. Ospreay sends him back into the ropes for another kick, wearing Kyle down to the mat as the crowd starts booing again. Ospreay fires off some more elbows to the back of Fletcher&#8217;s head until the ref calls for a break since Kyle is on the ropes. Ospreay retreats to the corner, sizing Kyle up for a Hidden Blade&#8230;but the challenger drops to the mat to narrowly evade the attack!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ospreay mouths off with Fletcher, allowing Kyle to cradle him for a two count&#8230;but Ospreay pops up for a Hidden Blade followed by the Storm Breaker! Cover by the champ, but Kyle gets his shoulder up. Ospreay heads to the corner to face his former friend head-on. Fletcher tells him how much he &#8220;f&#8211;king hates&#8221; the champ, who goes for a Hidden Blade&#8230;but Kyle counters with a backslide for the closest of two counts.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ospreay gathers enough strength to fire off another Hidden Blade, looking for a Tiger Driver. Fletcher manages to break free, but takes one more Hidden Blade followed by the Tiger Driver as Ospreay finally takes the win to retain the title!</p>



<h3 id="winner-via-pinfall-and-still-aew-world-champion-will-ospreay" class="wp-block-heading">Winner via pinfall and still AEW World Champion: Will Ospreay</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">United Empire joins Ospreay in celebrating the win as we see Fletcher get to the corner, propping himself against the turnbuckle to look at the man who got the best of him tonight. Ospreay gets to his feet, shaking hands and hugging his teammates as appropriate before getting one from Andrade (even after he reminds Ospreay he&#8217;s got that title shot for down the line). Fletcher leaves the ring by this point, and so do United Empire as the champ stands alone in the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Suddenly, someone dressed in all black with a mask blindsides Ospreay in the ring! It doesn&#8217;t take long to realize what&#8217;s happened, as it&#8217;s revealed that MJF attacked the champ with his &#8220;One True Championship&#8221; before United Empire chases him off. MJF escapes through the crowd as United Empire check on Ospreay, who took a bit of damage to his head and neck as Full Gear comes to a close.</p>



<h3 id="aew-full-gear-quick-results" class="wp-block-heading">AEW Full Gear Quick Results:</h3>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>AEW International Championship:</strong> Kazuchika Okada def. Adam Copeland</li>



<li><strong>AEW World Tag Team Championship:</strong> The Young Bucks def. Davis &amp; Doyle</li>



<li><strong>AEW World Trios Championship &#8211; Texas Death Match:</strong> Swerve Strickland &amp; The New Level def. Hangman Adam Page &amp; Brodido &#8211; <strong><em>TITLE CHANGE!</em></strong></li>



<li><strong>AEW Women&#8217;s World Tag Team Championship:</strong> Wrathlander def. The Brawling Birds &#8211; <strong><em>TITLE CHANGE!</em></strong></li>



<li><strong>AEW National Championship:</strong> Ilja Dragunov def. Tommaso Ciampa &#8211; <em><strong>TITLE CHANGE!</strong></em></li>



<li><strong>AEW Women&#8217;s World Championship:</strong> Mercedes Moné def. Marina Shafir</li>



<li><strong>Anarchy in the Arena:</strong> The Cut (Jay White, David Finlay, Clark Connors, Ace Austin, Colten Gunn, and Austin Gunn) def. Death Riders (Jon Moxley, Daniel Garcia, &amp; Gabe Kidd) &amp; The Conglomeration (Orange Cassidy, Kyle O&#8217;Reilly, &amp; Roderick Strong)</li>



<li><strong>AEW World Championship:</strong> Will Ospreay def. Kyle Fletcher</li>
</ul>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397439-aew-full-gear-results-11-14-26-anarchy-in-the-arena-title-matches-and-more/">AEW Full Gear Results – 11/14/26 (Anarchy in the Arena, title matches, and more!)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
